 5. ⚠️ Loud superintelligence warning 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Via X 

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The latest AI warning: Meta chief AI officer Alexandr Wang says in a 757-word essay on X that it's "hard to imagine a world where humanity can maintain control" over AI that improves itself without limits.

 "It is equally hard to imagine a world where humanity maintains control with superintelligence that is 1000x smarter and more capable than humans in every field," Wang wrote. Wang cited the recent AI-assisted proof of one of math's most famous unsolved problems — the Riemann hypothesis — as a sign that AI is already smart enough to tackle the world's hardest problems.

 That includes AI research. Wang expects models to become "superhuman at improving themselves — along with massively accelerating biological research, weapons research, economics research, and more." Read Wang's warning . 

 
 
