 6. 📊 Charted: AI&#x27;s $1.4 trillion year 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: JPMorgan. Chart: Noah Bressner/Axios JPMorgan projects AI data center spending will nearly double next year to $1.4 trillion.

 Growth will slow after that, though it will remain at levels that "would have been unfathomable two years ago," the analysts wrote. In all, the bank forecasts about $7 trillion in data center spending from 2027 through 2031. 
 
